  "faq": [
    {
      "_type": "faqItem",
      "answer": "Yes, if you want landscape over pampering. The islands are spectacular and a private boat makes them feel private. Labuan Bajo itself is a working harbour town, so plan to spend your time on the water, not in it.",
      "question": "Is Komodo a good place for a honeymoon?"
    },
    {
      "_type": "faqItem",
      "answer": "For a honeymoon, yes if the budget allows. It buys you the timing, which is what separates the Padar ridge at sunrise from the Padar ridge with forty other people on it. It is the best-value upgrade on the trip.",
      "question": "Should you charter a private boat in Komodo?"
    },
    {
      "_type": "faqItem",
      "answer": "Park entry uses a bundled ticket per route: around IDR 650,000 per person for the Komodo Island route, or around IDR 900,000 for routes including Rinca and Padar, booked ahead through the official app or your operator. The system has changed before, so confirm when booking.",
      "question": "How much are Komodo National Park fees in 2026?"
    },
    {
      "_type": "faqItem",
      "answer": "Roughly April to October, when seas are calmest and boat days are least likely to be cancelled. January and February are the worst months for weather disruption.",
      "question": "When is the best time for a Komodo honeymoon?"
    },
    {
      "_type": "faqItem",
      "answer": "Fly to Labuan Bajo, about 1 hour 15 minutes direct. It is the only sensible option: the sea alternative is a multi-day liveaboard, not a transfer. Take a morning flight, since afternoon delays are common.",
      "question": "How do you get from Bali to Komodo?"
    },
    {
      "_type": "faqItem",
      "answer": "Five days is the practical minimum for two water days plus a weather buffer. Seven lets you add a quiet island stay at the end, which is what turns a sightseeing trip into a honeymoon.",
      "question": "How many days do you need in Komodo?"
    },
    {
      "_type": "faqItem",
      "answer": "Komodo is easier to reach and more dramatic above water. Raja Ampat is far better below it, and much harder to get to. If this is your first trip east of Bali, Komodo is the more forgiving choice.",
      "question": "Is Komodo or Raja Ampat better for a honeymoon?"
    }
  ],
